SPEC-356a -- THE LICENSED-BACKLOG DIRECTED CELL, AND THE THREE FAIL PATHS
                        THAT HAD NO COMMITTED ARTIFACT
=========================================================================

WHAT THIS FILE IS. Four demonstrations, each produced by running the thing
rather than by reading it:

  PART 1  the licensed backlog (`topgun_or_prune_eligible_refs`) read NON-ZERO
          at sample instants on the repaired instrument -- the directed cell
          ADJ-7 rests on, with the pre-repair flat-zero census as its
          before-picture.
  PART 2  the exhaustiveness identity's RED, driven by a mutation (A2).
  PART 3  the arming witness firing in BOTH directions, exit 9 each (A3).
  PART 4  the `exit 2` refusals, all six of them, with their console output
          and their exit codes (A7a).

WHY IT EXISTS. Parts 2-4 were required by their acceptance criteria to be
RECORDED and were carried only as claims in the execution summary; a claim
about a fail path is exactly the thing this spec's two evidence gates exist to
distrust. Part 1 is the evidence for the repair those gates' own census
exposed the need for.

NOT A MEASUREMENT ARTIFACT. Every run below is a smoke cell or a unit test.
The basenames are ones no SPEC-356b cell can produce, the artifacts were
written to scratch directories, and nothing here is an input to any
classification.

WHY THIS FILE MAY SPELL THE INSTRUMENT-DEFECT LITERAL WHILE THE EG-2 ARTIFACT
MAY NOT. SPEC-356b's consumer greps are FILE-SCOPED: it counts the literal in
each cell's own `<cell>.harness-console.log` and in `spec356a-step0c-fixture.log`,
never across this directory. Parts 3 and 4 below are recordings of runs whose
whole purpose was to FIRE that defect, so the literal appears here as captured
output -- the thing it names actually happened. Adding a grep that reads this
directory as a whole would break that distinction and is not one of 356b's
checks.

================================================================================
PART 1 -- THE LICENSED BACKLOG, READ NON-ZERO AT SAMPLE INSTANTS
================================================================================

THE BEFORE-PICTURE (committed, spec356a-eager-registration.log): on the
pre-repair instrument the licensed backlog was recomputed AFTER the drain had
removed every eligible epoch, so it read a structural zero at every sample:

  topgun_or_prune_eligible_refs                [POPULATN] n=13 empty=0 min=0 max=0
  topgun_or_prune_ineligible_refs              [POPULATN] n=13 empty=0 min=0 max=2072

INVOCATION (verbatim, as run, on the repaired instrument):

  SDKROOT=$(/usr/bin/xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path) \
  SPEC356_SMOKE_DURATION=120 SPEC356_OUT_DIR=/tmp/spec356-fix-smoke2 \
    packages/server-rust/benches/soak_harness/evidence/spec356-prune.sh smoke

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
