  9     0          1034       2                7
  10    0          1034       2                7
  11    1000       996        2                8
  12    0          1069       3                9

READING IT. Rows 8 and 11 read 1000 -- one epoch's worth of refs at width
1000. The pre-repair emitter could not produce that number at any sample: its
recompute site ran after an UNBOUNDED drain had taken every ref it had just
counted. The split-recompute counter moves alongside, so these are fresh
computations and not a frozen sample.

AND THE HONEST BOUND, STATED HERE RATHER THAN LEFT TO BE DISCOVERED. Ten of
the twelve rows still read 0, and a second run of the same cell caught NO
non-zero sample at all (n=13, max=0). That is not the defect coming back --
it is the world: this prune sweeps on every OR_REMOVE (4,288 passes in 120 s
here), so a newly-licensed ref is drained within milliseconds and the backlog
is genuinely transient at width 1000 under this workload. The repair's claim
is therefore precise: a zero is now a READING rather than a CONSTRUCTION, and
a regime in which the prune cannot keep up -- the one Steps 3-4 exist to name
-- leaves a backlog that persists across sample instants and IS caught. A
10 s gauge sample of a transient quantity remains a lower bound on it, and
SPEC-356b reads L with that bound in view.

================================================================================
PART 2 -- A2: THE EXHAUSTIVENESS IDENTITY, SEEN RED
================================================================================

MUTATION. One exit is dropped from the ledger in the prune loop:

  -                    pass.matched_nothing += 1;
  +                    // MUTATION: exit dropped from the ledger

INVOCATION (verbatim, as run):

  SDKROOT=$(/usr/bin/xcrun --sdk macosx --show-sdk-path) \
  cargo test -p topgun-server --lib prune_exit_ledger_sums_to_considered

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
CAPTURED FAILURE (verbatim tail)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  
    left: 0
   right: 1
  note: run with `RUST_BACKTRACE=1` environment variable to display a backtrace
  
  
  failures:
      service::domain::crdt::tests::prune_exit_ledger_sums_to_considered
  
  test result: FAILED. 0 passed; 1 failed; 0 ignored; 0 measured; 1794 filtered out; finished in 0.21s
  
  error: test failed, to rerun pass `-p topgun-server --lib`

The identity is 'every considered ref left through exactly one exit'. With one
exit unrecorded the sum falls short by exactly the refs that took it (left 0,
right 1), which is the property TG-OR-006 names. The mutation was reverted and
the working tree verified clean before the next step.

================================================================================
PART 3 -- A3: THE ARMING WITNESS, FIRING IN BOTH DIRECTIONS
================================================================================

Direction 1 -- an ARMED cell whose child process is forced DISARMED. The
witness must catch the ABSENCE of series that arming requires.

  SPEC356_SMOKE_DURATION=45 SPEC356_OUT_DIR=/tmp/spec356-w1 \
  SPEC356_WITNESS_DEMO_ARMING=false spec356-prune.sh smoke

  arming witness:
    cell expects:        armed=yes
    TOPGUN_PRUNE_RECORD: false (on the child)
    topgun_or_prune_ lines in the scrape: 0
    pinned prune columns resolved:        0/40
    topgun_ormap_tombstone_bytes present: 2 line(s)
  INSTRUMENT DEFECT: arming witness: cell 'smoke' is ARMED but the scrape carries NO topgun_or_prune_ series -- the process that ran was DISARMED
  RESULT: INSTRUMENT DEFECT -- this run's series must not be recorded as evidence.
  -> exit status: 9

Direction 2 -- a DISARMED cell whose child process is forced ARMED. The witness
must catch the PRESENCE of series that disarming forbids.

  SPEC356_SMOKE_DURATION=45 SPEC356_OUT_DIR=/tmp/spec356-w2 \
  SPEC356_WITNESS_DEMO_ARMING=true spec356-prune.sh smokeoff

  
  arming witness:
    cell expects:        armed=no
    TOPGUN_PRUNE_RECORD: true (on the child)
    topgun_or_prune_ lines in the scrape: 89
    pinned prune columns resolved:        40/40
    topgun_ormap_tombstone_bytes present: 2 line(s)
  INSTRUMENT DEFECT: arming witness: cell 'smokeoff' is DISARMED but the scrape carries 89 topgun_or_prune_ line(s) -- the process that ran was ARMED
  RESULT: INSTRUMENT DEFECT -- this run's series must not be recorded as evidence.
  -> exit status: 9

Both directions exit 9 and both write INSTRUMENT DEFECT. A witness that could
only fail closed in one direction would pass a cell that ran armed while
labelled disarmed -- the control arm silently measuring the treatment.

